 Spatial Grounding for City-Scale 3D Scenes",128,"2026-10-14"],["2610.26659","SpatialScout: Can VLM Agents Actively Explore and Map 3D Scenes?",122,"2026-10-22"],["2609.02886","SolarWM: Open Data and Scalable Training for Long-Horizon Video World Models",115,"2026-09-03"]],"featured":[{"id":"2611.17336","date":"2026-11-14","title":"Back to Pixels: Lifting Latent Video Diffusion into Pixel Space","tldr":"PixVid fine-tunes a pretrained latent video diffusion model to generate every frame directly in pixels, matching its quality while enabling higher resolution, frame-accurate editing and one-frame control latency."},{"id":"2611.12870","date":"2026-11-14","title":"SWAM: Scaling World Action Models with Cross-Modal Alignment","tldr":"A 47,000-hour study of how to train world action models finds that detailed captions and mixing human egocentric video with handheld-gripper demonstrations best preserve video-model knowledge while learning robot control."},{"id":"2611.14488","date":"2026-11-13","title":"Is Your Robot's Memory Just a Clock? Temporal Shortcuts in Memory-Augmented VLA Policies","tldr":"Memory-augmented robot policies often track elapsed time rather than events, so a harmless pause makes them believe work was done; indexing memory by events recovers much of the loss."},{"id":"2611.12885","date":"2026-11-12","title":"World In-Context Learning for Agentic Robot Manipulation","tldr":"A frozen foundation model learns robot tasks by rehearsing in a simulator and writing lessons into a text memory, reaching 83.4% on RoboTwin 2.0 from one demonstration, over 20 points above trained policies."},{"id":"2611.12806","date":"2026-11-11","title":"Learning Heterogeneous Tactile Representation for General Dexterous Manipulation","tldr":"LingBot-Touch learns one touch representation across three kinds of tactile sensors from 5,000 hours of data, and its small frozen encoder raises real-robot success by 14 to 26 points."},{"id":"2611.09894","date":"2026-11-09","title":"Video-Coder: Reinforcing Agentic Coding for Video Generation","tldr":"Video-Coder trains a coding agent to build a 3D draft scene in Blender, which guides a video generator and raises physical plausibility scores on two benchmarks."},{"id":"2611.09892","date":"2026-11-09","title":"On Agentic Manipulation Policies","tldr":"Letting a general-purpose AI model write code that directly drives a robot arm, with no demonstrations or robot-specific training, beats leading specialist vision-language-action policies by a wide margin."},{"id":"2611.06905","date":"2026-11-06","title":"Reinforcement Learning Enables Scaling Generalist Robot Policy Improvement","tldr":"Fine-tuning a generalist robot policy with value-based reinforcement learning across many tasks improves it on unseen objects and scenes, which single-task fine-tuning does not."},{"id":"2611.06918","date":"2026-11-05","title":"From Pixels to Actions - Towards Native Vision-Language-Action Policies","tldr":"NEO-VLA drops the separate vision encoder from a robot policy and lets its action module read visual features from many backbone layers, beating encoder-based baselines on LIBERO."},{"id":"2611.00859","date":"2026-11-03","title":"Wave Forcing: Towards Speed-of-Light Streaming Video Generation","tldr":"Wave Forcing lets several video chunks denoise at once on different GPUs, with earlier chunks serving as cleaner context for later ones, reaching about 135 end-to-end frames per second on eight H200 GPUs."},{"id":"2610.40748","date":"2026-11-03","title":"WorldBridge: Bridging Video and Action for Task Generalization in World Action Models","tldr":"In a video-plus-action world model, videos of new tasks without action labels lift out-of-distribution success on RoboTwin 2.0 from 25% to 56%, and one labeled demonstration per task lifts it to 71%."},{"id":"2610.42146","date":"2026-11-02","title":"Hierarchical World Models with Implicit Dynamics","tldr":"ID-WM plans long tasks by using diffusion noise as an abstract action that picks reachable subgoals, while a second model converts each hop into precise actions."}]}